<div class="poster">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="headline">HAVE YOU SEEN THESE MEN?</div>

    <div class="photo-block">
      <div class="photos">
        <div class="photo-col">
          <div class="placeholder">[Photo: Lee Kuan Yew, profile portrait, black &amp; white]</div>
          <div class="caption-box">
            <div class="name">LEE KUAN YEW</div>
            <div class="details">
              Prime Minister of Singapore<br>
              Graduate from CAMBRIDGE<br>
              Worked for Japanese fascists in the 2nd World War.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="photo-col">
          <div class="placeholder">[Photo: Hussein Onn, in military-style uniform and cap, black &amp; white]</div>
          <div class="caption-box">
            <div class="name">HUSSEIN ONN</div>
            <div class="details">
              Prime Minister of Malaysia<br>
              Trained by the British army in Malaya,India,Middle-East<br>
              Graduate from LINCOLN's INN (London)
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="perp-title">PERPETRATORS OF CRIMES AGAINST THE<br>PEOPLE OF MALAYSIA AND SINGAPORE</div>
      <div class="perp-text">
        To maintain the interests of British and other foreign capital<br>
        and the local elites, THEY
      </div>
      <div class="perp-list">
        : SUPPRESS workers' and peasants' rights.<br>
        : BAN independent trade unions and student unions.<br>
        : MANIPULATE judicial&nbsp;&nbsp;process.<br>
        : SUPPRESS parliamentary democracy and press freedom.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="jail-headline">THEY JAIL AND KILL PEOPLE</div>

    <div class="british-connection-box">
      <div class="bc-title">THE BRITISH CONNECTION</div>
      <div class="bc-sub">
        RUBBER AND TIN from colonial Malaya were crucial to British<br>
        post-war recovery.
      </div>
      <div class="bc-content">
        <div class="placeholder bc-photo-left">[Photo: worker at rubber tapping / plantation labor]</div>
        <div class="bc-text">
          <p>"Without Malaya, the Sterling System, as we know it could not exist." Purcell</p>
          <p>A 12-year British Military Rule was imposed after the World War II to protect British economic interests.</p>
          <p>Repressive laws were first introduced by the British colonial regime, then further improved by the local elites.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="placeholder bc-photo-right">[Photo: soldiers with rifles in jungle setting]</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bc-bottom">
        Though formally 'independent', Britain CONTINUES to exert influence and control through
        <ul>
          <li>Domination of the economies</li>
          <li>Collaboration with the repressive regimes</li>
          <li>Cultural subversion</li>
          <li>Five-Power-Defence-Arrangement (U.K., Australia, New Zealand,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Malaysia and Singapore).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="picket-wrap">
      <div class="bottom-text" style="position:relative; z-index:1;">
        <div class="bottom-headline">
          BELIEVED TO BE IN LONDON ATTENDING<br>
          THE COMMONWEALTH P.M. CONF.<br>
          JUNE 8-16,1977
        </div>
        <div class="publisher-info">
          Published by&nbsp; COBRA and NUS<br>
          COBRA&nbsp; -Conference for Basic Human and Democratic Rights in the ASEAN alliance<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;6, Endsleigh Street&nbsp;&nbsp; London WC1
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="picket-triangle">
        <div class="picket-text">
          <span class="big">PICKET&nbsp; LEE AND HUSSEIN ONN</span><br>
          Place :&nbsp; Parliament Square, London SW1<br>
          Date :&nbsp; 9th June 1977<br>
          Time :&nbsp; 5 to 9 p.m.<br>
          SEND LETTERS/TELEGRAMS of protest<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;c/o Commonwealth Secretariat,<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Marlborough House,<br>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;London SW1.<br>
          Copies to COBRA.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
